---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Legal Documents | BlueFx Markets" description="Sample legal documents for the BlueFx Markets demonstration website." page="legal">
<main id="content">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Company / Legal Documents</p>
        <h1>Legal documents</h1>
        <p class="lede">Sample summaries for this demonstration, dated 17 November 2026. They are not a contract you can accept, and they do not open an account.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <article class="doc">
          <details open>
            <summary>Client Agreement</summary>
            <p>The sample agreement would sit between BlueFx Markets, Windhoek, and a client who has passed the demo profile. It would name the account type, lock the currency to NAD, and point at the MT5 client terminal as the place orders are sent. Bonus credit would be described as separate from cleared cash.</p>
            <p>Nothing on this website is that agreement. Registering on the login page stores nothing on a server.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
        <article class="doc">
          <details>
            <summary>Risk Disclosure</summary>
            <p>Forex, CFDs and synthetic indices can lose more than a small deposit when leverage is high. Premium leverage up to 1:2000 and Micro leverage up to 1:500 are the sharp end of that. A stop-out, even a zero stop-out, is not a promise that a position survives.</p>
            <p>Past sample hit rates on the signal bots are not a forecast. Most retail CFD accounts lose money. Namibia does not make that fact softer.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
        <article class="doc">
          <details>
            <summary>Order Execution Policy</summary>
            <p>Every account on the schedule is marked Market execution. The sample policy would say that BlueFx does not guarantee a fill at the price on the market watch, because those prices are simulated on this demo and a live price can move while the order is in flight.</p>
            <p>Spreads from 0–2 pips on Pro, or 0.5 pips on VIP and the synthetics accounts, are published minimums, not a quote that is always on the screen.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
        <article class="doc">
          <details>
            <summary>Privacy Policy</summary>
            <p>A live policy would cover the name, email, Namibian phone number, town and identity documents a client sends to support@bluefxmarkets.com. It would say the Windhoek desk keeps them to run the account and to meet KYC, and does not sell them.</p>
            <p>This demo form does not transmit those fields. If you type them, they stay in the browser until you leave the success message.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
        <article class="doc">
          <details>
            <summary>AML and KYC Policy</summary>
            <p>The sample standard asks for a Namibian ID or passport, a proof of address in Namibia, and a bank account or card in the same name. Deposits from a third party would be returned rather than credited. DPO payments that fail the name check would sit until the desk can see who sent them.</p>
            <p>Source of funds can be asked on deposits above N$50,000 in this sample policy. That figure is illustrative.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
        <article class="doc">
          <details>
            <summary>Conflict of Interest</summary>
            <p>A broker that is the counterparty to a CFD has a different interest from the client. The sample note would say so plainly, and would say that staff in Windhoek may not trade the client book ahead of a client’s order.</p>
            <p>Signal bots on this site are a display. Enabling one does not create an order and does not pay the desk a commission.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
        <article class="doc">
          <details>
            <summary>Complaint Handling</summary>
            <p>Complaints in this sample go first to support@bluefxmarkets.com with the account name and the CAT time of the issue. The desk would acknowledge them within two Windhoek business days and answer within ten.</p>
            <p>If the answer is not enough, the sample path points at the licence page, which explains that this site is a demonstration and not a live regulated complaint channel.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
        <article class="doc">
          <details>
            <summary>Cookie Policy</summary>
            <p>This demo does not set tracking cookies. The page remembers nothing except what your browser keeps while it is open. A live site would say which cookies run the login and which, if any, measure the Windhoek marketing pages.</p>
            <p>Last updated for this demonstration: 17 November 2026, Windhoek.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
